auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

docs {
  # MonaFindAuto API v1

  Every request in this collection sends `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` and
  `Accept: application/json`. The few open endpoints ignore the header.

  ## Getting a token

  Run **01-auth / Register** or **01-auth / Login**. Both have a post-response
  script that writes `token` into the active environment, so everything after
  them just works.

  ## The order that actually matters

  Registration leaves the account **Pending**, and a Pending account cannot
  check out. Run **01-auth / Verify phone** before anything under 04-orders,
  or you will get a 403 that looks like a permissions bug and is not.

  In a `local` environment the SMS provider is the log driver — the code is in
  `storage/logs/laravel.log`, or in `storage/logs/integration-fakes.log` when
  the fake provider is bound.
}
